],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"St. Thomas Orthodox Syrian Church is located in the Cantonment of Prayagraj in Uttar Pradesh in north India. The wooden building was completed in 1889 as the Garrison Church. In 1948 it was renamed as the St. Thomas Orthodox Syrian Church. The church is a parish in the Diocese of Delhi, Malankara Orthodox Syrian Church.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"St. Thomas Orthodox Syrian Church, Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Front_St_Thomas_Orthodox_Syrian_Church_Allahabad_Dec23_A7C_08492.jpg/1280px-Front_St_Thomas_Orthodox_Syrian_Church_Allahabad_Dec23_A7C_08492.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Front_St_Thomas_Orthodox_Syrian_Church_Allahabad_Dec23_A7C_08492.jpg/500px-Front_St_Thomas_Orthodox_Syrian_Church_Allahabad_Dec23_A7C_08492.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"This Photo was taken by Timothy A. Gonsalves. Feel free to use my photos, but pl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_St_Thomas_Orthodox_Syrian_Church_Allahabad_Dec23_A7C_08492.jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_shah_begum_s_tomb","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Shah Begum's Tomb","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.44235,"lng":81.82093},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_shah_begum_s_tomb","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":32,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["shahbegumstomb","prayagraj"],"summary":"Shah Begum' was the wife of Jahangir and the mother of Khurso Mirza. She was born as Man Bai and was the daughter of Raja Bhagwant Das, the ruler of Amer. She overdosed on opium in 1604, and the tomb was built in 1606. Designed by Aqa Reza, the elaborate calligraphy was executed by Mir Abdullah Mushkin Qalam. Shah Begum's Tomb is the principal tomb of the complex and occupies the central position.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg/1280px-Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg/500px-Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"juggadery","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allahabad,_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_(39649022981).jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_allahabad_high_court","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Allahabad High Court","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.45336,"lng":81.82081},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_allahabad_high_court","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.allahabadhighcourt.in/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":5,"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["allahabadhighcourt","prayagraj"],"summary":"It is the seat of Justice in Uttar Pradesh, and is the oldest high court in the country with largest strength of judges.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Allahabad_high_court.jpg/1280px-Allahabad_high_court.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Allahabad_high_court.jpg/500px-Allahabad_high_court.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Vroomtrapit at English Wikipedia","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allahabad_high_court.jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_university_of_allahabad_campus","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"University of Allahabad Campus","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.46696,"lng":81.86019},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_university_of_allahabad_campus","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.allduniv.ac.in/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":4,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["universityofallahabadcampus","prayagraj"],"summary":"The 4th oldest university of India, it has various neo-Gothic monuments. The university originally started as the Muir College in 1872. With the foundation of the Allahabad University in 1921 the Muir College merged with the newly formed university. The college was founded by William Muir, Lieutenant Governor of the North-West Provinces of India. The Muir College complete with domes and tower is b","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Au_science_faculty.jpg/1280px-Au_science_faculty.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Au_science_faculty.jpg/500px-Au_science_faculty.jpg","w":1200,"h":1849,"author":"Abhijeet Vardhan","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Au_science_faculty.jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_wv_bibi_tamolon_s_tomb","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Bibi Tamolon's Tomb","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.44244,"lng":81.81969},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_wv_bibi_tamolon_s_tomb","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":10,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["bibitamolonstomb","prayagraj"],"summary":"On the western side of the three tombs lies the lone tomb of Bibi Tamolon. Nothing much is known about the tomb or its occupant. The sandstone built octagonal tomb stands on a high plinth and is topped with a dome.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg/1280px-Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg/500px-Allahabad%2C_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_%2839649022981%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"juggadery","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allahabad,_Kusru_Bagh_42_-_royal_palms_(39649022981).jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_wv_victorial_memorial","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Victorial Memorial","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.45366,"lng":81.8492},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_wv_victorial_memorial","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":6,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["victorialmemorial","prayagraj"],"summary":"Victoria Memorial is not a memorial but a canopy, which once housed the imposing marble statue of Queen Victoria. The impressive marble canopy along with the statue was installed in 1905 and was inaugurated by Sir James John Digges La Touche, the governor of United Provinces of Agra and Oudh. In 1960s the statue of Queen Victoria was removed and shifted to the Municipal Museum in Lucknow. The cano","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg/500px-Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"कृष्ण कान्त शर्मा","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_wv_company_bagh","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Company Bagh","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":25.45371,"lng":81.84814},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_wv_company_bagh","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":5,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["companybagh","prayagraj"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"It is the place to experience the British era of Indian history. The park came up in 1870 during the visit of Prince Alfred (second son of Queen Victoria) and was named after him. It also came to be known as Company Bag. It is the largest park in Prayagraj and covers an area of 133 acres. Encircled in this park are Allahabad Museum (for details see Museum section), Victoria memorial and the public","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg/500px-Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"कृष्ण कान्त शर्मा","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Victoria_Memorial_16.jpg"}},{"id":"prayagraj_wv_khusro_bagh_gate_north","areaId":"prayagraj","name":"Khusro bagh gate (north)","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.44469,"lng":81.82187},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"prayagraj_wv_khusro_bagh_gate_north","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":2,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["khusrobaghgatenorth","prayagraj"],"summary":"This gate located on Station Road provides easy access and is more frequently used. This is a new gate and has no historic significence.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Prayagraj","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Info_Map_Khusro_Bagh_Allahabad_Jan24_A7C_08642.jpg/1280px-Info_Map_Khusro_Bagh_Allaha